 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current bounded finding: row/column counts can imitate the transform analogy
+
+On unchanged production source
+`67e83a7965329ac7be920d38120a4c2e0d0b9bb5e4762c7434e41bf5f6ae8f32`,
+rule `bfccb7008cc6`, a plausible feature shortcut fits a complete four-branch
+lesson: infer the first allowed transform whose row and column occupied-cell
+counts match B, rather than comparing every transformed A pixel with B; then
+apply that transform to C normally.
+
+The retained ordinary medium lesson uses seed 0, demonstration indices
+2, 3, 4, 5 and query index 6, without overrides. The demonstrations cover
+left-right flip, up-down flip, clockwise rotation and 180-degree rotation.
+The alternative fits all four outputs. On the query, A and B have identical
+row counts `[1,1,2]` and column counts `[1,2,1]`, despite differing pixels.
+The rival chooses identity instead of the intended left-right flip and changes
+two answer cells. All retained inputs pass `self_check`; the exact original
+grouping also passes `lesson_identifiable` with `[]`.
+
+These are consecutive ordinary per-puzzle draws. The standard episode assembler
+was not invoked, so this is not a claim that it emitted the grouping. Discovery
+was bounded to sixteen unique ordinary inputs (seeds 0 and 17, indices 0..7,
+medium) and four feature summaries: centroid, bbox, row/column projections and
+corner pixels. Only the row/column-projection counterexample is retained.
+
+`workspace/projection_probe.py` pins source and canonical program hashes and
+changes only the canonical A/B comparison to form a complete executable Racket
+alternative. Both programs label every retained demonstration, query and guard
+through the real protected Racket evaluator. Five saved canonical pairs also
+replay correctly: 17 protected evaluations, exit 0. Full original lesson,
+alternative answers, programs and per-cell differences are retained in
+`checks/5f8ebdb4bd9c/projection.json`. Command and verification receipts are
+`checks/5f8ebdb4bd9c/projection-command.json` and
+`checks/5f8ebdb4bd9c/projection-verify-command.json`; discovery is recorded in
+`checks/5f8ebdb4bd9c/feature-prefilter-command.json`.
+
+A distinct ordinary input, seed 0/index 7, rejects the rival: its correct command
+is up-down flip while the projection matcher chooses 180 degrees. Replacing the
+original up-down demonstration at index 3 with this guard preserves all four
+branches and refutes the selected shortcut. The repaired grouping still passes
+the existing lesson helper. Adding this executable rival and requiring such a
+distinguishing demonstration is a focused repair proposal; production was not
+changed. This finite result does not establish uniqueness against all programs.
+
+The prior exact-source clean audit remains recorded as `resolution: needs_triage`
+with accepted triage metadata and reviewer-reported checks. Its disposition is
+unchanged. The new finding concerns demonstration support, not canonical-label
+correctness, and does not grant approval or training admission.
